  "id": "kohler-effect",
  "term": "Köhler effect",
  "definition": "The Köhler effect is a proposed explanation for why people may show a motivation gain when working in a group. In the source, it is described as distinct from social compensation and contrasted with social loafing, and its role may differ depending on whether group members are lower or higher performers.",
